.Model/.Projection/.Source/.ViewModel (compiled + unit-tested headlessly by TeslaSync.App.Tests via explicit
<Compile Include> links); the .cs is the thin Fluent view exercised by the app build.

NOTE on the LiveMotorStatus duplicate: two LiveMotorStatus feature surfaces exist —
TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.LiveMotorStatus (full drivetrain reading: shift/power/regen/source/F+R rpm/
F+R torque/F+R motor temp/inverter/battery + HV-isolation prop, the DrivetrainHealth child) and
TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Driving.LiveMotorStatus (the DrivingDynamics subset). Because this page lives in
.Driving, the unqualified name resolves to the subset variant; the full drivetrain variant is bound by
fully-qualified type names (TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.LiveMotorStatus / .MotorLiveReading /
.ILiveMotorStatusSource) so the page reproduces the complete web LiveMotorStatus region, not the subset.

